From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitalii Apostolyuk <vitalii.apostolyuk@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:11:38 +0000
Subject: upstream-pr-3009: Ocarina of Time draws HDR on a Mac screen that can
 show it

nxnative PR #3009 (oxyp1e, open): Ocarina of Time asks vi::QueryDisplayHdrStatus every frame
and switches its window textures between RGBA8 (SDR) and RGB10A2 (HDR10) with its own tone
mapping. The host now answers from the window's screen (potential EDR headroom of 4 or more:
a MacBook Pro's XDR panel reports 16) and presents the HDR10 picture in extended dynamic
range. DM_HDR=auto|0 (launcher row "HDR", default from the profile key hdr, Ocarina only).

NXForge on top:
- an HDR10 picture takes the PR's pass (present_hdr_pipeline); every other picture keeps
  NXForge's present pass, its filters, anti-aliasing, pixel art and EDR highlights
- under HDR10 the present skips anti-aliasing, pixel art, filters, border fill and frame
  interpolation (they read gamma bytes); MetalFX keeps the picture's own format
- the layer is switched by EDR highlights' own switch (present_edr.inc nxf_edr_layer, which
  now also takes the HDR want), so the two never fight over the layer's format
- the present constants buffer stays NXForge's 44 floats; HDR10's sit at 8-11

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
